      "content": "Prioritizing pathways to citizenship and humanitarian processing is more likely to yield a stable, long-term solution. By creating legal avenues, the country can integrate immigrants into the economy and society, turning temporary arrivals into productive, tax-paying citizens. Overly aggressive enforcement, while seemingly decisive, often leads to human crises and fails to address the underlying economic needs for labor.",
